# PAM runs with NONE of this set.
#
# The project the app talks to is checked in at src/lib/project.ts — the URL,
# the publishable key, and the public address. That is deliberate: a build that
# fails because a dashboard field was left blank is a failure mode this project
# decided not to have, and the publishable key is designed to ship in browser
# JavaScript anyway. The access rules in packages/db are the boundary, and
# `pnpm --filter @pam/db test` is what proves it.
#
# Everything below is an OVERRIDE, for a staging project or a fork. Copy this to
# .env.local only if you need one.

# --- A different Supabase project ----------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- A different public address ------------------------------------------
# The base of every invite link that goes out by text.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

# --- Google Maps (§5.1) ---------------------------------------------------
# Restrict by HTTP referrer and bundle ID before using anywhere but localhost.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# --- Support line (§2.4) --------------------------------------------------
# First-paint fallback only. The live value is app_settings.support_phone, which
# an admin changes without a deploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_PHONE=

# --- Never here -----------------------------------------------------------
# The service role key and every Twilio credential belong in Supabase Edge
# Function secrets. They are not NEXT_PUBLIC_ anything, and a test fails the
# build if something shaped like one appears in src/lib/project.ts.
